    <string name="help_lists_title">Your lists</string>
    <string name="help_lists_text">This shows all to-do lists from Home Assistant. You switch the list by tapping the list name on the main screen.\n\nNext to each list you see its store. When you switch to a list, its items are sorted in the order of that store – on the phone and on the watch. Lists without their own store use the first store.\n\nCreating and deleting lists is only possible with the token of a Home Assistant administrator. New lists are created with the “Local To-do” integration and selected right away. Only such lists can be deleted – for other integrations (e.g. Shopping List, Google Tasks, Todoist) Home Assistant would remove the whole integration with all of its lists. Deleting a list removes all of its items.</string>
    <string name="help_markets_title">Stores and sections</string>
    <string name="help_markets_text">A store remembers in which order you walk through the sections of a shop and which sections it has. That way the list is sorted along your route through the shop.\n\nWhich store belongs to which list is set in the “Lists” tab; lists without a store use the first store. Here the selection field chooses which store you edit. “+” adds a store, empty or as a copy of an existing one. The pencil renames, the bin deletes; the last store is always kept.\n\nDrag sections by the handle into the right order. Disabled sections are hidden in the section selection for new or edited items, but stay visible in the shopping list when existing items use them. Everything is applied with “Save”.</string>
